0..75 Comment "// The iterated pair, twenty levels deep, in two spellings. Each level is a"
76..138 Comment "// record of two fields, and both fields hold the level below."
139..141 Comment "//"
142..221 Comment "// The unshared tree of the pair has 2^20 leaves, but the term has one node for"
222..299 Comment "// each level. A checker that walks each occurrence of a node walks the whole"
300..375 Comment "// tree. Without its memo, the core checker exceeds its step allowance from"
376..453 Comment "// depth 16 in the let spine and from `t18` in the definition spine. Thus the"
454..469 Comment "// depth is 20."
470..472 Comment "//"
473..548 Comment "// Each checker keeps a goal memo. The memo answers a goal that the checker"
549..623 Comment "// meets again in one step, so each spelling checks in steps linear in the"
624..701 Comment "// depth. The definition spine names each level by a declaration, and the let"
702..781 Comment "// spine binds each level to a name. At depth 20, the kernel checks `pair20` in"
782..851 Comment "// 87 goals and recalls 59, against 8,388,629 goals without its memo."
852..854 Comment "//"
855..932 Comment "// Limits: `gandr check --measure` refuses the artifact from depth 18, so the"
933..1011 Comment "// kernel\'s counts come from depths 1 to 17. The kernel has no step allowance,"
1012..1059 Comment "// so its walk without the memo also completes."
1060..1062 Comment "//"
1063..1117 Comment "// - see: #5719 — the goal memo of the core checker."
1118..1173 Comment "// - see: #5797 — the decoder\'s cap on expanded work."
1174..1252 Comment "// - see: `crates/core-checker-base/src/judgement/memo.rs` — the key and the"
1253..1280 Comment "//   binders that it reads."
1281..1357 Comment "// - see: `crates/kernel-core/src/lib.rs` § the memo\'s collapse law — the"
1358..1412 Comment "//   kernel\'s memo on the pair that the kernel builds."
